{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124508","id":4875859691,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIp-26w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124508.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124508/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124508/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124508/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b4bdc3b475a210ef2639791008bb3fdc0cb03ec7","number":124508,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix WaylandThread crashing when attention is called to a destroyed window","user":{"login":"skorpnok","id":6632336,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzIzMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6632336?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok","html_url":"https://github.com/skorpnok","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skorpnok/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\n\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\n\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\n-->\n\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\n- Closes #124493 \n\n## Additional information\nThe issue was caused by a lack of concurrency guards. Since the the attention mechanism was not fully implemented before godot never ran into the issue where attention was being called to a window that is also being destroyed. Specifically ``WaylandThread::window_destroy`` did not know if there are other reference that are potentially in use (in waiting callbacks in this case). And for ``WaylandThread::_xdg_activation_token_on_done``  there was no way to check if the window pointer was still valid.\n\nThis PR adds some locks and late deletion to ``WaylandThread::WindowState`` to prevent the use-after-free from happening. Note this touches quite a few places around WaylandThread as I had to move ``WindowState`` to it's own allocations to allow it to contain the required locks. There are probably more race-conditions in wayland thread but this PR fixes the specific regression.\n\n<!--\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\n-->\n","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-15T15:39:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T20:29:15Z","closed_